    "status": "present",
    "value": "Simulate the process literally. Work on a copy of the grid using 0 = healthy, 1 = active infection, 2 = walled. Each day, flood-fill every active region and record its cells, the set of distinct healthy cells it threatens and the number of walls (healthy neighbour sides). Pick the region with the largest threatened set, add its wall count to the answer and mark its cells 2. Every other region then turns its threatened cells to 1. Stop when there are no regions or the best region threatens nothing."
  },
